{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779567741,"nonce":"+mbXT/GIXMAvxzt5IHIE6OTV9lc=","title":"Generic graph worker execution for Studio training","message":"## Summary\n\nReplace Studio training worker bridge semantics with a generic execution path over serialized `GraphSpec` models, task data bindings, retained observables, and executable loss specs.\n\n## Context\n\nParent umbrella: `07c0ec9`.\n\nThe graph-template slice made `Network` and Simple Feedback templates executable through `GraphSpec`, but the worker still contains topology-specific bridge code for controller, plant, observation, and loss construction. The next implementation slice should execute the serialized graph boundary directly and use explicit task/loss/retention contracts instead of reconstructing a hidden `SimpleStagedNetwork`/plant path.\n\n## Contract\n\n- `GraphSpec` is the canonical execution composition boundary.\n- Leaf components may be causal, acausal, equational, ODE-based, solver-based, or otherwise opaque internally; they only need executable ports/state at the graph boundary.\n- `TaskSpec` and `TaskBindingSpec` are the only task data ingress contract.\n- `TrainingSpec.loss` lowers into executable objective terms.\n- `GraphSpec.retained_observables` plus loss/artifact requirements lower into a retention plan.\n- Unsupported display-only nodes fail preflight with actionable errors; the worker must not hide unsupported nodes behind special type branches.\n\n## Implementation Checklist\n\n- Add generic compile/preflight for graph, task bindings, retained observables, loss terms, trainability, and checkpoint layout.\n- Add selected graph tracing for ports, edges, graph outputs, recurrent carries, task data, and state paths.\n- Replace worker-side controller/plant/observation/loss reconstruction with graph execution and retained-observable loss evaluation.\n- Keep event names usable for Studio while making payloads selector-keyed.\n- Serialize full graph checkpoints and retained-observable artifacts in run manifests.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Tiny full-graph training run executes without `_derive_worker_graph_lowering` or `_extract_graph_params`.\n- Unsupported component nodes fail before JIT with selector/node path information.\n- Loss terms and manifest artifacts are produced from lowered plans, not hard-coded tracking/effort/smoothness branches.\n\nRelated: `07c0ec9`, `0e1cd8c`, `4f835cb`, `a1036a6`.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}